  "notes": "An intransitive verb describing a curly, wavy, or crinkled state. Most commonly used for hair and noodles. The past participle {縮|ちぢ}れた functions as an adjective meaning \"curly\" or \"crinkled.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {髪|かみ}が{縮|ちぢ}れる: hair becomes curly/frizzy\n- {縮|ちぢ}れ{毛|げ}: curly hair (as a noun)\n- {縮|ちぢ}れ{麺|めん}: curly noodles\n- {縮|ちぢ}れた{葉|は}: crinkled leaves\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive. The transitive form is {縮|ちぢ}らす (to make curly, to curl something).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {巻|ま}く: to curl, to wind (active curling action)\n- くせ{毛|げ}: naturally curly/wavy hair (noun describing hair type)\n- {縮|ちぢ}む: to shrink (focuses on getting smaller, not curling)",
